give. And it's either like, all right, it's a good shot.

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:15.580
Or if you miss it by a, by a centimeter, it's a terrible shot.

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:16.680
It doesn't, the ball doesn't go anywhere.

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:19.160
And at first I was kind of like, well, that, that's kind of annoying.

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:22.380
The more I thought about it, I mean, I guess that is kind of like real golf.

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:25.040
You have a very little space that you need to hit exactly.

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:27.820
And if you miss a little bit, you, it changes your shot a lot.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:31.820
So like, I started to kind of, what's that?

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:34.480
I guess I've never had that.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:39.620
I had that issue a lot of like, different from when, from, from what I remember from NES golf.

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:43.280
Sam, you can correct me if I'm wrong because you played it more recently, but I remember

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:46.880
having a lot more leeway and that maybe it was just, maybe I was just bad at this game,

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:50.540
but I noticed in this game, if I missed just a little bit, it would go nowhere.

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:51.820
Oh, definitely.

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:54.800
Yeah. You have way more leeway in NES golf.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:59.220
And I mean, sometimes if you really mess up, the ball goes straight up in the air and

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:01.780
then come right back down, but you don't miss it ever.

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:06.560
And Joe, I get what you're saying about, you know, if you miss it, if you miss the theoretical

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:11.580
ball a little bit, like, yes, the shot would be awful, but I refuse to also believe that

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:18.200
you have the skillset of a pro golf player and then can also make like such terrible mistakes

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:21.280
like that in the same instance by just being off a little bit.

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:27.320
Like the window just needed to be bigger, bigger here regardless, because like, I think

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:31.100
what Sean was talking about where like auto hits for you, like that is definitely something

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:32.940
that happened for me in the putting mode.

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:37.640
And, um, and I, I was actually like nice to see it there because that's the last thing

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:41.100
I want to worry about is like hitting the ball correctly while I'm like playing mini golf.

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:46.520
But like in some respects, yeah, you do have to make sure that you're like hitting the theoretical

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:49.840
golf ball because if you've ever been to a driving range and you're not a regular golf

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:53.480
player, you're going to miss that golf ball a lot of times, you know, even though it's

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:57.760
right there on the tee. Like it, it feels like tee ball where you're like, how could I possibly miss this thing?

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:03.840
But it will happen. I just think that that that was just another moment in this game where things were just

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:06.400
a little too strict that, uh, for a video game.

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:10.480
You're not trying to simulate being an amateur golfer.

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:12.180
You can do that yourself.

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:14.380
Exactly. Yeah.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:19.180
Especially because it's, it's done with, it's illustrated with a meter with that, that

00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:24.820
moves at a random speed and like random compared to what the fact that there is no meter in

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:29.840
real life. Like if it was illustrated with something that translated more to golf, then I can understand

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:30.740
it being that difficult.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:36.380
But since it's like, oh, we need to get how, you know, figure out how well, how good you can

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:41.620
time this press of the a button with this meter that's moving.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:42.940
Like, well, it doesn't really translate the golf.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:44.780
So like that part shouldn't be what's difficult.

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:47.080
Sorry. That was a mouthful, but I hope everyone.

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:48.820
No, I understood it.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:50.020
Yeah. Loud and clear.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:52.960
You know, it's not even the biggest disappointment in this game though.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:59.000
That award goes to the moment where you leave the title screen with its super groovy

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.160
Kirby's dreamland inspired music.

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:06.880
And then you just wind up going to the golf course and it's the same track over and over

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:12.420
again. And I'd rather just have NES golf soundtrack, which I'll remind you was nothing.

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:15.160
I thought that a lot too.

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:16.800
NES golf was like relaxing.

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:19.600
Yeah. This song was so annoying.

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:23.320
Just the same. It's like not even interesting at all.

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:26.520
There's no. There's like nothing to it.

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:29.700
Someone just kind of was like, all right, hum something real quick and I'll turn into

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:32.980
a song. It's like something like that.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:34.440
And I was like, all right, that's good enough.

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:35.760
Well, I just tuned it out.

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:41.720
I can't even remember the sound of it, but that sort of plays into the rest of like

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:42.960
what's sort of wrong with this game.

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:49.080
I mean, it would have been more in character for this game to be silent because it also

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.260
just doesn't have any personality anywhere.

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:56.900
It's just like, like I said earlier, it's just like a menu based golf game.

00:19:57.240 --> 00:20:00.300
And I did like that.

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:09.240
It had sort of the cross section of showing the showing elevation changes across the course.

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:14.800
Uh, that was sort of like a cool image thing that was also useful.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:20.900
But otherwise, like there's nothing that there's nothing like there's no personality to this game.

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:23.180
Yeah. But the data is there.

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:27.040
And I get what you're saying, Sean, with like it just being a series of menus, because it

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:30.240
feels like ultimately that's what they're going for, because things that we have never

00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:32.580
seen before, I don't think any of the other games had handicap.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:34.060
So like that has it there.

00:20:34.180 --> 00:20:37.500
Sure. But even the detail that they put on the scorecard is pretty good.

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:42.200
And then finally, like a long complaint that I've had with the other golf games is that you'd

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:45.980
never really know how much distance you have to go to the hole.

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:49.540
And finally, like we got that here in this game.

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:51.880
So like they give you more than enough information.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:57.340
It's just, it's just about as boring as real golf as the end result.

00:20:57.340 --> 00:21:01.940
Like if you're trying to make golf as boring as it seems on TV for someone like me, you've

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:03.040
done it. You've done it.

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:07.680
They've succeeded. This is coming from Mike, who, who I think voted.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.640
Didn't he vote like NES golf, like number two of 1985?

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:13.080
That's true. It's like one of your favorite games.

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:19.460
I think as NES golf understood the arcadey moments of golf and also came up with the

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:23.640
remind you with the whole system that all these other golf games are based on.

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:26.020
We haven't like that was the first time that it was ever done.

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:30.500
So I think that's really cool that they wound up coming up with this solution that all these

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:38.020
other people have found. And I think that like the changes that both Lee Trevino and Pandai Golf here have made

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:41.040
are not like changes in the appropriate direction.

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:43.800
Like, yes, they might simulate more things.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:49.460
Like I think for whatever reason, Pandai Golf has an actual fluctuating wind system that

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:51.180
is just not realistic to life.

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:55.600
All of a sudden, it's like, you know, it's one meter to the left, zero meters nowhere,

00:21:56.180 --> 00:21:57.260
nine meters up front.

00:21:57.380 --> 00:22:01.020
And it's like, does that stop once I select my club?

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:02.960
Because I still have a good amount of time.

00:22:03.020 --> 00:22:05.120
And now you've removed the wind information.

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:08.180
So like, did it just end wherever I selected?

00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:11.760
And now that's like, that's the that's the wind for the rest of the course?

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:13.460
Or is it still fluctuating?

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:14.440
And I just have no idea.

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:17.720
And I happen to be in the middle of a tornado that's going to sweep up my ball.

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:20.080
Apparently, there's a windy course.

00:22:20.240 --> 00:22:22.640
So I would imagine that there are gusts.

00:22:22.640 --> 00:22:28.320
But like the one time you should be able to see the wind information is when you're in

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:29.740
like about to take your swing.

00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:34.740
But like once exactly like I would imagine it goes away that it pauses where you left it.

00:22:34.740 --> 00:22:39.000
Like it's I guess like the whole that just wouldn't make any sense.

00:22:39.340 --> 00:22:47.180
I give them enough credit to say that they're giving you the correct information at the time of this swing.

00:22:47.560 --> 00:22:50.080
But then it's only ever like an advantage though, right?

00:22:50.220 --> 00:22:51.940
It's only ever to your benefit.

00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:57.800
You might as well just wait until you see a great wind in your favor if it's going to change so rapidly.

00:22:57.800 --> 00:23:09.020
Like I understand that certain holes are built different so that so that like if you're on a whole number seven or something like it is designed so that the wind is going to the left.

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:15.220
But if it's still going to fluctuate wildly, you might as well wait till it's not like seven meters in your direction.

00:23:15.480 --> 00:23:17.200
And the ball is going to like not travel as far.

00:23:17.300 --> 00:23:22.140
And now you're thinking like a regular golfer that might not hit into the wind if he can help it.

00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:24.140
So, OK, no point taken.

00:23:24.160 --> 00:23:25.400
That was good. That was well thought.

00:23:25.620 --> 00:24:10.660
Yeah. Why is golf going for realism on the NES of all systems like we have just started with the return of video games?

00:24:11.080 --> 00:24:18.720
Um, it's it's early on the graphics aren't like able to be as detailed and they wouldn't know that obviously but like interesting in hindsight here.

00:24:18.720 --> 00:24:21.860
Why are they all going for this realistic simulation style?

00:24:22.120 --> 00:24:28.020
Why can't we get just a like a lunar pool style mini golf game that's really silly?

00:24:28.340 --> 00:24:31.880
Why are we always getting, you know, this is Pebble Beach.

00:24:32.040 --> 00:24:36.740
This is Japan and USA's premier golf courses with different recognizable characters.

00:24:36.760 --> 00:24:38.640
Like when are we going to get something fun?

00:24:42.440 --> 00:24:44.440
Like, cause you're talking about it in hindsight.

00:24:44.720 --> 00:24:55.060
It's not like they should have said like, yeah, we should just wait until like 2018 when we can put something on like the, the PS4 or to be actually realistic.

00:24:55.060 --> 00:25:08.540
I think that there, that everybody throughout the history of video games has been trying to get realism down, like whether or not they succeed or not, it's more likely in the later generations.

00:25:08.540 --> 00:25:15.760
Um, but I do agree that I would like a more, more of like a golf story sort of thing.

00:25:16.420 --> 00:25:25.100
It, where it's more like, let's just have fun with the concept of golf and have it be this arcade fun thing.

00:25:25.340 --> 00:25:30.580
Uh, I'm surprised we haven't seen that, but I, I cannot fault them for wanting to be realistic.

00:25:31.560 --> 00:25:33.260
I, I, I agree with you on that.

00:25:33.360 --> 00:25:39.140
And I also think though, that it's just a matter of precedent to like, you haven't seen anything like that before.

00:25:39.380 --> 00:25:44.700
So an idea like that, if you're a developer is like weird and scary where it's like, well, what if nobody likes that?

00:25:44.740 --> 00:25:46.200
Like no one's ever done anything like that.

00:25:46.420 --> 00:25:48.300
If you're thinking like, Oh, we're gonna make a golf game.

00:25:48.560 --> 00:25:51.840
Probably just the first thing everyone thinks of is like, okay, let's just make golf.

00:25:52.780 --> 00:25:57.120
You know, like until you've seen like until some more things start kind of slowly breaking into it.

00:25:57.120 --> 00:26:00.640
And then more people are like, Oh, people like these quirky, weird things when they're talking about sports too.

00:26:01.420 --> 00:26:04.100
Then, um, then I feel like we'll see more of that stuff.

00:26:04.560 --> 00:26:06.520
Yeah. Cause what other sports game?

00:26:06.600 --> 00:26:10.100
I mean, so you said lunar pool and like, maybe we had that one hockey game.

00:26:10.260 --> 00:26:14.800
That was, uh, that was like a little less realistic in more in the art style really.

00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:18.340
But like most of the sports games we've had are like all going for realism.

00:26:19.040 --> 00:26:20.860
Yeah. Double dribble is pretty arcade.

00:26:21.060 --> 00:26:22.240
Yeah, I'd say so.

00:26:22.240 --> 00:26:27.100
But it's not, not in the same regard as, uh, as a lunar pool.

00:26:27.300 --> 00:26:32.800
It was still trying to simulate the rules of, uh, of basketball the best they could.

00:26:32.980 --> 00:26:38.700
It just ended up being a much more action packed game because it's basketball and not golf.

00:26:40.180 --> 00:26:43.820
Yeah. My only answer to that is just, you know, again, my biases here.

00:26:43.820 --> 00:26:53.820
I am putting golf in the like bowling billiards darts category and not the baseball, you know, basketball football category.

00:26:53.820 --> 00:27:02.640
So I guess that's where I'm branching off with my, like, they should just make these games fun, not focus on simulation because they're at the, at the root core of it for me.

00:27:02.640 --> 00:27:04.860
Like, I want these games to be fun.

00:27:05.060 --> 00:27:08.900
Whereas like, you know, for baseball, it's like, Oh, bring on the simulation.

00:27:08.900 --> 00:27:16.760
Like I'd love to control a team through a full season, you know, even if it is on crappy hardware, like that's, that's just my own bias here.

00:27:16.880 --> 00:27:23.460
I just think it is strange that a game that like you could theoretically like the putting system is all you need.

00:27:23.580 --> 00:27:26.360
A mini golf game would be great on this system.

00:27:26.600 --> 00:27:28.020
And I'm not sure we're going to get it.

