All right. I have, then I'm, I'm still prone to agree with you though.

00:27:38.080 --> 00:27:54.480
I, I don't think, uh, it seems that sports games have, have sort of just fit that one mold and we're not going to see like, even like, even in the other category that you described of, of like basketball, baseball, et cetera, et cetera.

00:27:54.480 --> 00:27:59.300
We're not going to see like a backyard baseball or something like that.

00:27:59.380 --> 00:28:01.460
It's just going to be simulation after simulation.

00:28:01.740 --> 00:28:03.060
I want them to prove me wrong though.

00:28:03.280 --> 00:28:11.900
I mean, if anything, I know this is super Nintendo, but we might see something like a Kirby's dream course or something like that, which isn't like supposed to be golf, but it's, it's golf.

00:28:12.020 --> 00:28:13.460
It's just silly, goofy golf.

00:28:14.360 --> 00:28:16.020
And like, maybe we'll see stuff more like that.

00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:22.300
It's just like cartoony and not necessarily golf, but it's like hit the ball towards the target in funny ways.

00:28:22.300 --> 00:28:24.180
Oh, yeah.

00:28:25.140 --> 00:28:27.400
Oh, yeah.

00:28:42.800 --> 00:28:45.540
Oh, yeah.

00:28:54.260 --> 00:28:55.300
Did you guys read the manual?

00:28:55.920 --> 00:29:02.220
I did. Did you like all the like nice drawings and detailed descriptions that they had going on?

00:29:02.360 --> 00:29:04.300
There's a lot of information here too.

00:29:04.440 --> 00:29:10.580
Like speaking of data, there's just, they really wanted you to know everything about this game without ever having to play it.

00:29:10.620 --> 00:29:12.860
I could almost play the game in my mind based off of the manual.

00:29:13.520 --> 00:29:15.060
That's just golf, man.

00:29:15.460 --> 00:29:17.240
Like it, that they will.

00:29:17.780 --> 00:29:25.560
I remember when I was, uh, but my, my dad made me watch a video describing a golf course.

00:29:25.560 --> 00:29:35.120
And like, they had segments of like talking about each hole and all of the interesting things about that hole.

00:29:35.740 --> 00:29:46.900
Like it was telling you a story about going from the, uh, the driving green or whatever the bucket, the T going from the T to the hole.

00:29:46.900 --> 00:29:48.380
It's sort of like this.

00:29:48.660 --> 00:29:51.980
So it's just sort of falling in line with the culture of the game.

00:29:52.680 --> 00:29:54.480
I didn't enjoy reading it.

00:29:55.100 --> 00:30:03.940
Yeah. I was gonna say, um, page 13 in the manual actually reminds me of like 11th grade math with the graph paper and stuff.

00:30:04.320 --> 00:30:06.640
More than it ever does remind me of a video game.

00:30:06.640 --> 00:30:08.440
Yeah. I'm not sure why that's there.

00:30:08.800 --> 00:30:17.040
Um, but it's, you know, it's, it's appreciated that it almost makes you seem like you're reading a textbook.

00:30:17.360 --> 00:30:21.100
That's cool. To me, it looks like it's like information on like a style doc.

00:30:21.100 --> 00:30:23.920
Like when I plug those numbers in, it's going to give me like specific colors.

00:30:24.980 --> 00:30:29.840
Or, uh, it's the, uh, it's the illustrations on the golden record of the Voyager.

00:30:32.060 --> 00:30:42.960
And, and now I'm just being mean, but if you go to page four, how to play the game, uh, it tells you start in bold and then title screen.

00:30:42.960 --> 00:30:46.280
And then next to that, an asterisk with title music.

00:30:46.280 --> 00:30:49.660
I'm, I'm just not even, this is all sounding like gibberish to me.

00:30:50.020 --> 00:30:51.300
What do you mean? Start.

00:30:51.620 --> 00:30:53.700
It sounds like start the title screen.

00:30:53.880 --> 00:30:55.280
Like the title music.

00:30:55.460 --> 00:31:03.660
What is that? Like, it sounds like it's like partially a manual and also partially like some of the documents they use.

00:31:03.880 --> 00:31:06.380
Yeah. It's like instructions to make the game.

00:31:07.120 --> 00:31:08.220
Yeah. All right.

00:31:08.300 --> 00:31:10.780
This is where the title is and we're going to put the music there.

00:31:10.900 --> 00:31:13.340
So we got to asterisk that so we don't forget.

00:31:14.820 --> 00:31:16.960
I agree. I think that's what this is.

00:31:17.460 --> 00:31:18.660
Yeah. It's wild.

00:31:18.840 --> 00:31:35.840
Cause it's almost like the start in bold means like a whole series of things that I feel like if they're trying to explain this to someone who's not familiar with video games, they're failing here because they're really telling you like plug the NES into a TV, put the cartridge in and turn the power on.

00:31:35.840 --> 00:31:38.340
That'll start in bold.

00:31:38.500 --> 00:31:40.060
And then you'll get to the title screen.

00:31:40.240 --> 00:31:43.800
Don't be alarmed if there's title music during the title screen.

00:31:44.840 --> 00:31:46.660
Finally, you can push start.

00:31:46.660 --> 00:31:48.460
They do. They do say push start.

00:31:48.540 --> 00:31:58.180
This way, you know, that it's about using your controller, but then they just start explaining other parts of the sub menus and the options between them going into a lot more detail.

00:31:58.180 --> 00:32:08.260
So I think this thing really just needed some good old fashioned tables in Microsoft Word style, you know, like just to explain like what each column is supposed to be.

00:32:08.260 --> 00:32:11.060
And you know, by the end of the manual, they sort of have that.

00:32:11.060 --> 00:32:13.660
I mean, they don't have lines, but they do have a table.

00:32:14.040 --> 00:32:26.160
Uh, so over, yeah, over the course of the author's, um, writing experience, he did figure out how to, how to put together, uh, some Excel docs, I think.

00:32:26.480 --> 00:32:31.720
Oh my God. Actually, if you overlay page 13 over page four, it points everything out of it.

00:32:32.080 --> 00:32:33.380
It's so funny.

00:32:33.520 --> 00:32:34.380
That is so good.

00:32:36.560 --> 00:32:41.040
You know, it is a nice touch though, with that subtle master's green color.

00:32:41.040 --> 00:32:46.280
That they use across the, uh, the whole entire manual that, you know, you get that jacket.

00:32:46.580 --> 00:32:50.220
If you win the masters, that's like the same color here.

